{
 "duration": 24.448,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "You sweat all the way up, then freeze at the top. Here's why.",
   "start": 0.3,
   "end": 3.55
  },
  {
   "text": "Climbing in a warm jacket soaks your shirt.",
   "start": 3.85,
   "end": 6.214
  },
  {
   "text": "On the summit, the wind hits that wet layer and pulls the heat right out of you.",
   "start": 6.414,
   "end": 10.813
  },
  {
   "text": "The fix is layers. Start a little cool, and take the warm layer off before you climb.",
   "start": 11.163,
   "end": 16.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Keep a fleece in your pack, and put it on the moment you stop.",
   "start": 16.468,
   "end": 19.394
  },
  {
   "text": "Dry on the way up, warm at the top.",
   "start": 19.744,
   "end": 21.817
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next cold hike.",
   "start": 22.216,
   "end": 24.248
  }
 ],
